00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:04.180
Leah: If a child or young person seems
to be depressed, it's important to

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.720
talk to them, to try to find out what's
troubling them and how they're feeling.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.950
Whatever is causing the problem,
it should be taken seriously.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:16.119
But first we need to know that there
is something wrong, and how to identify

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:19.220
the signs or symptoms of ‘Depression’
in children and young people.

00:00:20.509 --> 00:00:23.040
Let’s look at some of the signs
and symptoms of depression

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.560
in children and young people.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.649
Rhiannon: Feeling sad, in a low
mood that doesn’t go away, or being

00:00:28.679 --> 00:00:30.440
irritable or grumpy all the time.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:34.989
Constantly feeling tired,
sleeping more than usual or maybe

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.390
having trouble sleeping all.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.290
Interacting less with friends
and family and not being

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.880
interested in things in general.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:44.099
Eating less than usual or overeating
and having big changes in weight.

00:00:44.099 --> 00:00:47.660
Unable to relax or being more lethargic
than usual or unable to feel emotions.

00:00:48.099 --> 00:00:50.970
Lacking confidence or talking
about feeling worthless.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.539
Self-harming, or even
talking about suicide.

00:00:55.309 --> 00:00:59.070
Leah: We can see from these signs and
symptoms that depression and anxiety which

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:02.660
we have looked at previously are very
similar in the way the present themselves.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.749
This is because some children and
young people with anxiety also

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.850
develop depression and vice versa.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:12.789
Rhiannon: If children or young people
are resistant to discussing their

00:01:12.789 --> 00:01:16.830
feelings or admitting that they may be
depressed, they should be encouraged

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.690
to talk to someone they trust, such as
a family member, a friend or someone

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:27.400
at school or should see their GP and
or be referred to specialist services.

